---
/* Roots & Routes from your GEDCOM. An Atlas page with the Atlas menu, but NOT the Base layout: Base carries the visitor counter, the ad slot,
   Google Fonts and the language script, none of which this page may have (the file never leaves the device; the meta CSP below enforces it).
   The menu list is shared with Base (src/lib/nav.js); the page's own files live in public/roots/. */
import { nav } from "../../lib/nav.js";
import { u } from "../../lib/url.js";
const here = Astro.url.pathname;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<!-- The privacy promise, enforced by the browser rather than only stated: scripts, styles and data come from this site only; nothing may be
     sent anywhere else; no forms, no third-party anything. This page has no analytics and does not use the site layout (which carries a counter and ads): it takes only the site's menu, from src/lib/nav.js, and the menu script in /js/nav.js. -->
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<title>Roots &amp; Routes from your GEDCOM</title>
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="roots.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="site">
  <div class="wrap sitein">
    <a class="brand" href={u("/")}>Record <em>Atlas</em></a>
    <button class="burger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="drawer" aria-label="Menu"><span class="bars" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
    <nav class="topnav" aria-label="Main">
      {nav.map(([label, links]) => (
        typeof links === "string"
          ? <a class:list={["menulink", here === u(links) ? "on" : ""]} href={u(links)}>{label}</a>
          : <details class="menu"><summary>{label}</summary><div class:list={["panel", links.length > 14 ? "long" : ""]}>{links.map(([h, l]) => h === null ? <span class="ph">{l}</span> : <a href={u(h)} class={here === u(h) ? "on" : ""}>{l}</a>)}</div></details>
      ))}
      <a class="findbtn" href={u("/add/")}>Add source</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
  <div class="drawer" id="drawer" hidden>
    <div class="wrap">{nav.map(([label, links]) => (
      typeof links === "string"
        ? <div class="dgrp"><a href={u(links)} class={here === u(links) ? "on" : ""}>{label}</a></div>
        : <div class="dgrp"><span class="gl">{label}</span>{links.map(([h, l]) => h === null ? <span class="gl gl2">{l}</span> : <a href={u(h)} class={here === u(h) ? "on" : ""}>{l}</a>)}</div>
    ))}
      <div class="dgrp"><span class="gl">Contribute</span><a href={u("/add/")}>Add a source</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<header class="top">
  <h1>Roots &amp; Routes</h1>
  <p class="lede">Drop in your family tree file and see it drawn on the Atlas: every place tied to its country, its flag and who ruled it that year.</p>
</header>

<main>
<section id="start">
  <div class="promise" role="note">
    <h2>Your file never leaves this computer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It is read and drawn by code running in this browser tab. It is not uploaded, not stored on a server and not seen by anyone.</li>
      <li>So you do not have to find it again, the last few files you open are kept in this browser only, on this device and never online. Forget one, or all, with a click, or untick the box under the file picker and nothing is kept.</li>
      <li>This page has no analytics, no cookies and no third-party scripts, and the browser is told not to let it contact any other site.</li>
      <li>To place your people it downloads the Atlas's own place files for the countries your tree mentions. Our server can see which countries were asked for; it never sees your file or a name from it.</li>
      <li>People who may be alive are shown on your own screen. The shareable export leaves them out, and you can hide them with one tick.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div id="drop" class="drop" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Choose a GEDCOM file">
    <p class="big">Drop a <b>.ged</b> file here</p>
    <p>or <label class="pick">choose one<input id="file" type="file" accept=".ged,.gedcom,text/plain" hidden></label></p>
    <p class="small">GEDCOM 5.5, 5.5.1 or 7, from MyHeritage, Ancestry, FamilySearch, Family Tree Maker and the rest. Big files are fine: 15,000 people takes about ten seconds.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="or"><button id="sample" class="link">or try an invented sample family</button></p>
  <p class="small or"><label><input type="checkbox" id="autokeep" checked> Keep the last files I open on this device, in this browser only</label></p>
  <div id="recent" class="recent" hidden>
    <h2>Kept on this device</h2>
    <ul id="recentlist"></ul>
    <p class="small">Saved in this browser only; they never leave it and are not part of online sync. <button id="rall" class="link">Forget all</button></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="busy" hidden>
  <div class="spin" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <p id="busymsg" role="status" aria-live="polite">Starting…</p>
</section>

<section id="work" hidden>
  <p id="stale" class="err" role="alert" hidden>Your browser is running a mix of old and new copies of this page's code, so results may be wrong (people missing from the search, for example). Reload with the cache switched off, or open the page through <code>scripts/serve-local.py</code>.</p>
  <div class="bar">
    <div id="chips" class="chips"></div>
    <label class="small hidel"><input type="checkbox" id="hideliving"> Hide living people</label>
    <details class="mh" id="mhbox"><summary><span class="mhbtn">MyHeritage and Ancestry links <span id="mhsum" class="mhsum">off</span></span></summary>
      <div class="mhbody"><p>Paste a profile or tree link for any one person from your MyHeritage tree. Everyone in this file then gets links back to it. Nothing is sent.</p>
      <input id="mhin" type="text" placeholder="https://www.myheritage.com/profile-…" aria-label="A MyHeritage profile or tree link for one person in this file">
      <p id="mhstat" role="status" class="small"></p>
      <p class="small"><b>Ancestry</b> · <label>site <select id="mhanc" aria-label="Which Ancestry site the links open"><option value="com.au">ancestry.com.au</option><option value="com">ancestry.com</option><option value="co.uk">ancestry.co.uk</option><option value="ca">ancestry.ca</option></select></label></p>
      <p id="ancstat" role="status" class="small"></p></div>
    </details>
    <nav class="tabs" role="tablist">
      <button role="tab" data-tab="tree" aria-selected="true">Tree</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="report">Import report</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="review">Places to review <span id="rcount" class="count"></span></button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="work">Workbench <span id="wcount" class="count"></span></button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="fix">Fix list <span id="fxcount" class="count"></span></button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="offer">Offer places</button>
      <button role="tab" data-tab="export">Export</button>
    </nav>
    <button id="keep" class="link" title="Keep this file in this browser so you can reopen it with one click. It stays on this device. The last few files are kept automatically unless you untick the box on the start screen.">Keep on this device</button>
    <button id="again" class="link">Open another file</button>
  </div>

  <div id="p-tree" class="panel"><iframe id="viewer" title="Roots and Routes views of your tree"></iframe></div>
  <div id="p-report" class="panel" hidden></div>
  <div id="p-review" class="panel" hidden>
    <div class="rbar">
      <input id="rfilter" type="search" placeholder="Filter places" aria-label="Filter places">
      <span id="rnote" class="small"></span>
    </div>
    <div id="rlist"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="p-work" class="panel" hidden>
    <h2>Workbench</h2>
    <p>Fix and add to your tree here. Nothing changes in your original: your edits are listed below, drawn on the tree straight away, and written into the new file only when you
    <button class="link" data-goto="export">export</button>. They live in this page only, so export before you close it.</p>
    <p id="wflash" class="flash" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
    <div class="wbar">
      <input id="wfind" type="search" placeholder="Find a person: a name, or a record number (I123)" aria-label="Find a person">
      <span class="small whint" id="whint">Matches open right here. Or press <b>Add a year</b> beside anyone below.</span>
    </div>
    <div id="wres"></div>
    <div id="wedit" class="wpanel" hidden>
      <div class="wphead"><h4 id="wname"></h4><button type="button" class="link" id="wclose">Close</button></div>
      <div class="wpbody">
        <div class="wpinfo">
          <p id="winfo" class="small"></p><p id="wmh" class="small"></p>
          <div id="whelp"></div>
          <div id="wlook"><h4>Look this person up elsewhere</h4><p id="wsends" class="small"></p><ul id="wlinks" class="llist"></ul></div>
        </div>
        <div class="wforms">
          <form id="wdate" class="wform"><label>Birth <input name="birth" placeholder="e.g. ABT 1850"></label><label>Death <input name="death" placeholder="e.g. 12 MAR 1910"></label><button class="btn">Save dates</button></form>
          <form id="wnote" class="wform"><label>Add a note <textarea name="text" rows="3"></textarea></label><button class="btn">Add the note</button></form>
          <form id="wsrc" class="wform"><label>Add a source <input name="title" placeholder="Title, e.g. Parish register of St Mary, 1850"></label><label>Link <input name="url" placeholder="https://… (optional)"></label><label>Page or entry <input name="page" placeholder="(optional)"></label><button class="btn">Add the source</button></form>
          <p id="werr" class="err" role="alert" hidden></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <details class="wlist" id="wd-undrawn" open>
      <summary><b>Not drawn yet</b> <span id="wundn" class="count"></span> <span class="small">People with no year, so no place on the tree. A year puts them on it.</span></summary>
      <div id="wundrawn" class="wcols"></div>
    </details>
    <details class="wlist" id="wd-merge">
      <summary><b>Maybe the same person</b> <span id="wmgn" class="count"></span> <span class="small">Same name and sex, born within two years, not related. Marking a pair merges nothing: it writes a link between the two records.</span></summary>
      <div id="wmerge"></div>
    </details>
    <details class="wlist" id="wd-edits" open>
      <summary><b>Your edits</b> <span id="wedn" class="count"></span></summary>
      <div id="wedits"></div>
    </details>
  </div>
  <div id="p-fix" class="panel" hidden>
    <h2>Fix list</h2>
    <p class="small">Work down each list in the tree you keep elsewhere: copy, paste, tick. Ticks and "left as is" stay in this page unless you ask to keep them: tick the box below, or save the decisions to a file. Each row says why, what to do next, and what the Atlas holds for that place, year and name. “Generate PDF” opens your browser’s own print window over a copy made here: choose “Save as PDF”. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
    <div class="ftool">
      <label class="small"><input type="checkbox" id="fliving" checked> Include living people</label>
      <input id="ffilter" type="search" placeholder="Filter by name or place" aria-label="Filter the fix list">
      <label class="small"><input type="checkbox" id="fcollapse"> Fold the Atlas notes</label>
      <label class="small">Ancestry links go to <select id="fanc" aria-label="Which Ancestry site the outside-search links use"><option value="com.au">ancestry.com.au</option><option value="com">ancestry.com</option><option value="co.uk">ancestry.co.uk</option><option value="ca">ancestry.ca</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="fbar" role="group" aria-label="Save or share the fix list">
      <span class="fbl">Take it with you</span>
      <button class="ibtn" id="fpdf" title="Opens your browser’s print window over a print-ready copy made on this device. Choose “Save as PDF”."><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 9V3h10v6M7 17H4v-7h16v7h-3M7 14h10v7H7z"/></svg><span>PDF</span></button>
      <button class="ibtn" id="ftext" title="Download the fix list as a plain text file"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v14H6zM14 3v4h4M9 12h6M9 16h6"/></svg><span>Text</span></button>
      <button class="ibtn" id="fcsv" title="Download the fix list as a CSV file, for a spreadsheet"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M4 10h16M4 15h16M10 5v14"/></svg><span>CSV</span></button>
      <span class="fbsep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="fbl">Your ticks</span>
      <button class="ibtn" id="dec-save" title="Save your ticks and “left as is” choices to a file"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4h11l3 3v13H5zM8 4v5h7V4M8 20v-6h8v6"/></svg><span>Save</span></button>
      <button class="ibtn" id="dec-load" title="Load ticks and choices you saved earlier"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 7a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5l2 2h8a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v9a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"/></svg><span>Load</span></button>
      <button class="ibtn ibtn-del" id="dec-forget" title="Forget the decisions kept on this device"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 7V4h4v3M6 7l1 13h10l1-13M10 11v6M14 11v6"/></svg><span>Forget</span></button>
      <input type="file" id="dec-file" accept="application/json,.json" hidden>
    </div>
    <div class="dec">
      <label class="small"><input type="checkbox" id="dec-on"> Remember my decisions on this device</label>
      <span class="small" id="dec-said"></span>
    </div>
    <p class="small">What is kept for matching is a scrambled fingerprint of each row, with the day (not encryption), so the same tree finds its decisions again. For <a href="../my-research/#fixes">My research</a> a short summary is kept too: the file name, how many fixes are left of each kind, and the place texts as typed in your file. People are only counted, never named. All of it stays in this browser; switching the box off, or “Forget what is kept”, removes it.</p>
    <div id="fsecs"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="p-offer" class="panel" hidden>
    <h2>Offer places back to Record Atlas</h2>
    <p>Optional, and nothing is ticked. Places this page could not read, or that you chose by hand, can help the Atlas learn them. Only the <b>place text</b> goes into the
    message: no names, no dates, no people, no counts, no file name. This page sends nothing. You tick the places you want to offer, read the message below, and send it from your
    own email or copy it. Places used only by living people are never listed.</p>
    <p id="oheld" class="small"></p>
    <p><button class="link" id="onone">Tick none</button> · <button class="link" id="oall">Tick all without a number in them</button> · <span id="ocount" class="small"></span></p>
    <div id="olist"></div>
    <h3>The message</h3>
    <textarea id="opreview" rows="10" readonly aria-label="The message that would be sent"></textarea>
    <p><a id="omail" class="btn" aria-disabled="true">Open in my email</a> <button class="btn" id="ocopy">Copy the message</button> <a id="ofile" class="link" download="places-for-record-atlas.txt">Download it</a> <span id="osaid" class="small" role="status"></span></p>
    <p class="small">An address with a number in it (a street, a plot) is left unticked because it can point at a home. Trim it to the town if you want to offer it: the text boxes are editable.</p>
  </div>
  <div id="p-export" class="panel" hidden>
    <h2>Export your GEDCOM, improved</h2>
    <p>Your own file, line for line, with only the changes you choose. Nothing is dropped or rewritten without being listed in a change log, and
    nothing leaves this page: the new file is made here and saved by your browser.</p>
    <fieldset id="xmode" class="xmodes">
      <legend>What to change</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="xm" value="enriched" checked> <b>Enriched</b> · adds coordinates and an Atlas id under each place that was matched exactly or that you picked. No existing line is changed. The safest choice.</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="xm" value="cleaned"> <b>Cleaned</b> · as enriched, and the places you picked on the review screen replace the old place text (the old text is kept beside it).</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="xm" value="shareable"> <b>Shareable</b> · as cleaned, and living people are reduced to a bare “Living” record, their family events removed, so you can send it to a relative. Read the change log: a living person named in a way we cannot recognise stays.</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="xm" value="faithful"> <b>No changes</b> · your file again, as it was.</label>
    </fieldset>
    <p><button id="xgo" class="btn">Make the file</button> <span id="xbusy" hidden>Working…</span></p>
    <div id="xout" hidden>
      <p id="xsum"></p>
      <p><a id="xfile" class="btn" download>Download the GEDCOM</a> <a id="xlog" class="link" download>Download the change log</a></p>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Programs differ. Putting the new file into Ancestry, MyHeritage or Family Tree Maker usually makes a new tree rather than updating the old one, and
    they may ignore the coordinates. This has been checked only by reading the new file back here, not yet in another program.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<p id="err" class="err" role="alert" hidden></p>
</main>

<footer>
  <p>Place names and coordinates: <a href="https://www.geonames.org/" rel="noopener">GeoNames</a> (CC BY 4.0). Regimes, flags, events and record collections: the Record Atlas.
  This is a prototype: it can be wrong, and a place it cannot read is shown for you to decide, never guessed.</p>
</footer>
<script is:inline src="/js/nav.js"></script>
<script is:inline src="js/app.js" type="module"></script>
</body>
</html>
